# Beacon v1 — Master Implementation & Engineering Plan

> **Revision 2** — incorporates the senior DevOps red-team audit. Three findings accepted, two corrected. See §0 for the verdicts and the reasoning behind each. **No product feature was removed to satisfy the audit.**

## Context

`/Users/torgodly/codeing/Beacon` is currently an unmodified **Laravel 13.23 React starter kit** (single `init` commit): Inertia 3, React 19 + React Compiler, Tailwind 4, shadcn/ui, Lucide, Fortify (2FA + passkeys), Wayfinder typed routes, PHPStan level 7, Pint, PHPUnit. No Beacon code exists yet.

We are building **Beacon** — a self-hosted, single-server control panel / PaaS for Ubuntu 24.04 (and 22.04) that provisions and manages Nginx vhosts, multi-version PHP-FPM, Node/Bun SSR apps, MySQL, Redis, Supervisor, Cron and Let's Encrypt **natively, without Docker**, from a modern React UI.

### Decisions locked in this session

| Decision | Choice | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Panel datastore | **SQLite** (`/opt/beacon/panel/shared/beacon.sqlite`, WAL) | No circular dependency — stopping the managed MySQL from the Services widget must not kill the panel |
| Panel cache / queue / locks | **Redis** | Avoids SQLite write contention; gives us `Cache::lock()` for per-site deploy mutexes |
| Live output transport | **Polling now, Reverb-ready** | Log writes go through an `OutputStream` contract; the UI reads a byte-offset endpoint. Reverb becomes a decorator later, no UI change |
| Git integration | **User-created GitHub App via manifest flow** | Full API: repo/branch picker, App-level webhook, Deployment + Commit Status API. Fallbacks: SSH deploy keys, and SHA-polling auto-deploy |
| Panel exposure | **Domain optional, IP:8443 fallback** | `install.sh` takes `--domain`; otherwise self-signed on `:8443`, with an "Attach panel domain" upgrade path in Settings |
| **OS user model** | **`beacon` (sites) + `beacon-panel` (panel)** | *Revised by audit.* `beacon` holds **zero sudo**. See §0.1 |

