## 3. Nginx & Supervisor Configuration Templates

Templates live in `resources/views/nginx/*.blade.php` and `resources/views/supervisor/*.blade.php`, rendered by `NginxTemplateRenderer` / `SupervisorTemplateRenderer` and piped to the wrappers on stdin.

### 3.0 Global includes (written once by `install.sh`)

```nginx
# /etc/nginx/conf.d/beacon-global.conf
map $http_upgrade $connection_upgrade {   # required by every reverse-proxy vhost
    default upgrade;
    ''      close;
}
server_tokens off;
client_body_timeout 30s;
gzip on; gzip_vary on; gzip_proxied any; gzip_comp_level 5; gzip_min_length 256;
gzip_types application/javascript application/json application/xml image/svg+xml text/css text/plain text/xml;
```

```nginx
{{-- resources/views/nginx/partials/acme.blade.php --}}
# Shared ACME webroot — works before the app is deployed, and for every site type.
location ^~ /.well-known/acme-challenge/ {
    root /var/www/beacon-acme;
    default_type "text/plain";
    allow all;
}
```

```nginx
{{-- resources/views/nginx/partials/ssl.blade.php --}}
ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/{{ $lineage }}/fullchain.pem;
ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/{{ $lineage }}/privkey.pem;
ssl_trusted_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/{{ $lineage }}/chain.pem;
include /etc/letsencrypt/options-ssl-nginx.conf;
ssl_dhparam /etc/letsencrypt/ssl-dhparams.pem;
add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000" always;
```

> **Certbot runs `certonly --webroot`, never `--nginx`.** Beacon owns the vhost completely and renders the `443` block itself; letting the certbot Nginx plugin rewrite it would mean the next regeneration silently drops TLS.
>
> **HTTP/2 syntax:** Ubuntu 24.04 ships nginx 1.24, where the form is `listen 443 ssl http2;`. nginx ≥ 1.25.1 wants a separate `http2 on;`. `NginxService::http2Directive()` runs `nginx -v` once, caches, and emits the correct form.

### 3.a Laravel (PHP-FPM)

```nginx
{{-- resources/views/nginx/laravel.blade.php --}}
# ─── Managed by Beacon — site: {{ $site->name }} ───
server {
    listen 80; listen [::]:80;
    server_name {{ $serverNames }};
    @include('nginx.partials.acme')
@if ($certificate)
    location / { return 301 https://{{ $site->name }}$request_uri; }
}
server {
    @if ($http2Inline) listen 443 ssl http2; listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    @else              listen 443 ssl; listen [::]:443 ssl; http2 on; @endif
    server_name {{ $serverNames }};
    @include('nginx.partials.ssl', ['lineage' => $certificate->lineage])
@endif

    root {{ $site->path }}{{ $site->web_directory }};
    index index.php index.html;
    charset utf-8;

    add_header X-Frame-Options        "SAMEORIGIN" always;
    add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"    always;
    add_header Referrer-Policy        "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" always;

    client_max_body_size {{ $site->client_max_body_size }};

@foreach ($redirects as $redirect)
    if ($host = '{{ $redirect->domain }}') {
        return {{ $redirect->redirect_status_code }} $scheme://{{ $redirect->redirect_to }}$request_uri;
    }
@endforeach

    location / { try_files $uri $uri/ /index.php?$query_string; }
    location = /favicon.ico { access_log off; log_not_found off; }
    location = /robots.txt  { access_log off; log_not_found off; }
    error_page 404 /index.php;

    location ~ \.php$ {
        fastcgi_pass unix:/run/php/php{{ $site->php_version }}-fpm-{{ $site->poolName() }}.sock;
        fastcgi_split_path_info ^(.+\.php)(/.+)$;
        include fastcgi_params;
        # $realpath_root resolves symlinks — required for the releases/current layout
        fastcgi_param SCRIPT_FILENAME $realpath_root$fastcgi_script_name;
        fastcgi_param DOCUMENT_ROOT   $realpath_root;
        fastcgi_hide_header X-Powered-By;
        fastcgi_read_timeout 60;
        fastcgi_buffers 16 16k;
        fastcgi_buffer_size 32k;
    }

    location ~ /\.(?!well-known).* { deny all; }   # blocks .env and .git, keeps ACME

    access_log /var/log/nginx/{{ $site->name }}-access.log;
    error_log  /var/log/nginx/{{ $site->name }}-error.log error;
}
```

### 3.b Next.js / Nuxt (reverse proxy)

```nginx
{{-- resources/views/nginx/proxy.blade.php --}}
upstream beacon_{{ $site->upstreamName() }} {
    server 127.0.0.1:{{ $site->proxy_port }};
    keepalive 16;
}
server {
    listen 80; listen [::]:80;
    server_name {{ $serverNames }};
    @include('nginx.partials.acme')
@if ($certificate)
    location / { return 301 https://{{ $site->name }}$request_uri; }
}
server {
    @if ($http2Inline) listen 443 ssl http2; listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    @else              listen 443 ssl; listen [::]:443 ssl; http2 on; @endif
    server_name {{ $serverNames }};
    @include('nginx.partials.ssl', ['lineage' => $certificate->lineage])
@endif

    client_max_body_size {{ $site->client_max_body_size }};

    # Immutable build assets served from disk — never wake the Node process
@if ($site->type === 'nextjs')
    location /_next/static/ { alias {{ $site->path }}/.next/static/;
        expires 365d; add_header Cache-Control "public, immutable"; access_log off; }
@else
    location /_nuxt/ { alias {{ $site->path }}/.output/public/_nuxt/;
        expires 365d; add_header Cache-Control "public, immutable"; access_log off; }
@endif

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://beacon_{{ $site->upstreamName() }};
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade    $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection $connection_upgrade;   # from beacon-global.conf
        proxy_set_header Host              $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP         $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For   $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host  $host;
        proxy_read_timeout 60s; proxy_connect_timeout 10s; proxy_buffering on;
    }

    access_log /var/log/nginx/{{ $site->name }}-access.log;
    error_log  /var/log/nginx/{{ $site->name }}-error.log error;
}
```

**Port allocation:** `PortAllocator` picks the lowest free port in `3000–3999`, guarded by a unique index on `sites.proxy_port` *and* a live `ss -ltn` check, inside `Cache::lock('beacon:port-alloc')`.

### 3.c Static site

```nginx
{{-- resources/views/nginx/static.blade.php --}}
server {
    listen 80; listen [::]:80;
    server_name {{ $serverNames }};
    @include('nginx.partials.acme')
@if ($certificate)
    location / { return 301 https://{{ $site->name }}$request_uri; }
}
server {
    @if ($http2Inline) listen 443 ssl http2; listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    @else              listen 443 ssl; listen [::]:443 ssl; http2 on; @endif
    server_name {{ $serverNames }};
    @include('nginx.partials.ssl', ['lineage' => $certificate->lineage])
@endif

    root {{ $site->path }}{{ $site->web_directory }};   {{-- /dist, /out, /build, / --}}
    index index.html index.htm;

    add_header X-Frame-Options        "SAMEORIGIN" always;
    add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"    always;

