### 4.2 `ProcessRunner` — the one place commands are executed

Three exits from the panel: **as itself**, **as root via a wrapper**, **as `beacon` via `beacon-run`**.

```php
<?php

namespace App\Services\System;

use App\Contracts\OutputStream;
use Symfony\Component\Process\Exception\ProcessTimedOutException;
use Symfony\Component\Process\Process;

class ProcessRunner
{
    public const SITE_USER  = 'beacon';
    public const PANEL_USER = 'beacon-panel';

    /** @param list<string> $command  @param array<string,string> $env */
    public function run(
        array $command, ?string $cwd = null, array $env = [], int $timeout = 60,
        ?string $input = null, ?OutputStream $stream = null,
    ): ProcessResult {
        $process = new Process($command, $cwd, $env + $this->baseEnv(), $input, $timeout);
        $process->setIdleTimeout(null);
        $startedAt = hrtime(true);

        try {
            $process->run($stream ? fn (string $t, string $c) => $stream->append($c) : null);
        } catch (ProcessTimedOutException) {
            return ProcessResult::timedOut($process, $this->elapsedMs($startedAt));
        }

        return ProcessResult::from($process, $this->elapsedMs($startedAt));
    }

    /**
     * Invoke a ROOT wrapper. Config content travels on STDIN — never in argv.
     * @param list<string> $args
     */
    public function sudoRoot(SudoWrapper $wrapper, array $args, ?string $stdin = null, int $timeout = 300): ProcessResult
    {
        return $this->run(['sudo', '-n', $wrapper->path(), ...$args], timeout: $timeout, input: $stdin);
    }

    /**
     * Execute AS THE SITE USER. Runas target is `beacon` (unprivileged), the
     * wrapper takes zero arguments, and the whole job spec goes over stdin —
     * so there is no argv surface and no sudo env plumbing.
     *
     * @param list<string> $argv  @param array<string,string> $env
     */
    public function asSite(
        array $argv, string $cwd, array $env = [], int $timeout = 120,
        ?OutputStream $stream = null, bool $oomExpendable = false,
    ): ProcessResult {
        return $this->run(
            command: ['sudo', '-n', '-u', self::SITE_USER, '/opt/beacon/bin/beacon-run'],
            timeout: $timeout,
            input: json_encode(compact('cwd', 'argv', 'env') + ['oom_expendable' => $oomExpendable],
                               JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR),
            stream: $stream,
        );
    }

    /** @return array<string,string> */
    private function baseEnv(): array
    {
        return ['HOME' => '/home/beacon-panel', 'USER' => self::PANEL_USER,
                'PATH' => '/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin'];
    }

    private function elapsedMs(int|float $t): int { return (int) ((hrtime(true) - $t) / 1_000_000); }
}
```

`SiteFilesystem` wraps `beacon-fs` for the panel's reads/writes inside `/home/beacon` (site `.env`, deploy scripts, Supervisor log tails) — canonicalised paths, prefix-checked, content on stdin.

### 4.3 `PhpExtensionService` — the cPanel-style toggle

Three states: **not installed** (offer `apt install`), **installed + disabled**, **installed + enabled**. The FPM restart is *debounced* so ten checkboxes restart FPM once.

```php
<?php

namespace App\Services\Php;

use App\Models\{PhpExtension, PhpVersion};
use App\Services\System\{ProcessRunner, SudoWrapper};
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\File;
use RuntimeException;

class PhpExtensionService
{
    /** Extensions Beacon will apt-install → package suffix. @var array<string,string> */
    public const INSTALLABLE = [
        'redis' => 'redis', 'imagick' => 'imagick', 'gd' => 'gd', 'bcmath' => 'bcmath',
        'pdo_mysql' => 'mysql', 'pdo_pgsql' => 'pgsql', 'intl' => 'intl', 'zip' => 'zip',
        'swoole' => 'swoole', 'mbstring' => 'mbstring', 'curl' => 'curl', 'xml' => 'xml',
        'soap' => 'soap', 'sqlite3' => 'sqlite3', 'apcu' => 'apcu',
        'memcached' => 'memcached', 'igbinary' => 'igbinary', 'xdebug' => 'xdebug',
    ];

    /** Never disableable — Laravel and the panel need these. */
    public const LOCKED = ['json','openssl','mbstring','tokenizer','ctype','fileinfo','opcache'];

    /** @var array<string,true> versions needing an FPM restart at request end */
    private array $dirty = [];

    public function __construct(private readonly ProcessRunner $runner) {}

    /** Reconcile the DB with disk: mods-available = installed, fpm/conf.d symlink = enabled. */
    public function sync(PhpVersion $version): void
    {
        $available = collect(File::glob("/etc/php/{$version->version}/mods-available/*.ini"))
            ->map(fn (string $p) => basename($p, '.ini'))->values();

        $enabled = collect(File::glob("/etc/php/{$version->version}/fpm/conf.d/*.ini"))
            // conf.d entries carry a load priority prefix: "20-redis.ini"
            ->map(fn (string $p) => preg_replace('/^\d+-/', '', basename($p, '.ini')))
            ->filter()->flip();

        foreach ($available->merge(array_keys(self::INSTALLABLE))->unique() as $name) {
            $version->extensions()->updateOrCreate(['name' => $name], [
                'label'        => $name,
                'apt_package'  => isset(self::INSTALLABLE[$name])
                    ? "php{$version->version}-".self::INSTALLABLE[$name] : null,
                'is_installed' => $available->contains($name),
                'is_enabled'   => $enabled->has($name),
                'is_core'      => in_array($name, self::LOCKED, true),
                'last_synced_at' => now(),
            ]);
        }
    }

    public function enable(PhpExtension $extension): void
    {
        $version = $extension->phpVersion;

        if (! $extension->is_installed) {
            $this->install($extension);          // apt-get install also enables it
        } else {
            // phpenmod -v 8.3 -s ALL redis → symlinks mods-available into every SAPI's conf.d
            $result = $this->runner->sudoRoot(SudoWrapper::Php,
                ['ext-enable', $version->version, $extension->name]);

            if ($result->failed()) {
                throw new RuntimeException(
                    "Could not enable {$extension->name} on PHP {$version->version}: {$result->errorOutput()}");
            }
        }

        $extension->update(['is_installed' => true, 'is_enabled' => true]);
        $this->markDirty($version);
    }

    public function disable(PhpExtension $extension): void
    {
        if ($extension->is_core) {
            throw new RuntimeException("{$extension->name} is required by Beacon and cannot be disabled.");
        }

        $result = $this->runner->sudoRoot(SudoWrapper::Php,
            ['ext-disable', $extension->phpVersion->version, $extension->name]);

        if ($result->failed()) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Could not disable {$extension->name}: {$result->errorOutput()}");
        }

        $extension->update(['is_enabled' => false]);
        $this->markDirty($extension->phpVersion);
    }

    private function install(PhpExtension $extension): void
    {
        if (! array_key_exists($extension->name, self::INSTALLABLE)) {
            throw new RuntimeException("{$extension->name} is not an installable extension.");
        }

        // apt can be slow on a cold mirror — this runs inside a queued job, not a web request.
        $result = $this->runner->sudoRoot(SudoWrapper::Package,
            ['ext-install', $extension->phpVersion->version, $extension->name], timeout: 600);

        if ($result->failed()) {
            throw new RuntimeException(
                "apt failed installing {$extension->apt_package}: {$result->combinedOutput()}");
        }
    }

    /** Coalesce N toggles into one FPM restart, flushed after the response is sent. */
    private function markDirty(PhpVersion $version): void
    {
        if (isset($this->dirty[$version->version])) {
            return;
        }

        $this->dirty[$version->version] = true;

        app()->terminating(function () use ($version): void {
            // Pool + module changes need a full restart; reload does not re-read conf.d.
            $this->runner->sudoRoot(SudoWrapper::Php, ['fpm-restart', $version->version], timeout: 120);
            unset($this->dirty[$version->version]);
        });
    }
}
```

### 4.4 `NginxService::saveRaw()` — the critical safety path

```php
public function saveRaw(Site $site, string $contents): void
{
    $result = $this->runner->sudoRoot(SudoWrapper::Nginx, ['write', $site->name], stdin: $contents);

    // 65 = the wrapper already rolled the previous config back in
    if ($result->exitCode() === 65) {
        throw ValidationException::withMessages([
            'contents' => NginxErrorParser::humanize($result->errorOutput()),
        ]);
    }

    if ($result->failed()) {
        throw new RuntimeException("nginx write failed: {$result->errorOutput()}");
    }

    $site->update(['nginx_customized' => true, 'nginx_managed_hash' => hash('sha256', $contents)]);
    $this->reload();
    activity()->on($site)->log('nginx.saved');
}
```

`NginxErrorParser::humanize()` turns

```
nginx: [emerg] unknown directive "proxy_pas" in /etc/nginx/sites-available/example.com:34
```

into `{ line: 34, directive: 'proxy_pas', message: 'unknown directive' }`, which the React editor renders as an inline gutter marker on line 34 — the UI requirement from spec §6.

### 4.5 `DeploymentService` — step-by-step execution

```php
public function run(Deployment $deployment): void
{
    $site = $deployment->site;

    // One deploy per site. A push storm queues; it never interleaves.
    $lock = Cache::lock("beacon:deploy:{$site->id}", self::SCRIPT_TIMEOUT + 60);

    if (! $lock->get()) {
        $deployment->update(['status' => 'cancelled', 'failed_step' => 'lock']);
        return;
    }

    // The panel owns this file handle — no cross-user access on the 1s polling path
    $stream = new FileOutputStream($deployment->log_path);   // /var/log/beacon/deployments/<uuid>.log

    try {
        $deployment->update(['status' => 'running', 'started_at' => now()]);
        $site->update(['deployment_status' => 'running']);
        $this->github->inProgress($deployment);

        $this->step($stream, 'Fetching source',        fn () => $this->fetchSource($site, $deployment, $stream));
        $this->step($stream, 'Running deploy script',  fn () => $this->runScript($site, $stream));
        $this->step($stream, 'Normalising permissions',fn () => $this->fixPermissions($site, $stream));
        $this->step($stream, 'Restarting processes',   fn () => $this->restartProcesses($site, $stream));

        $this->finish($deployment, 'success', 0);
        $this->github->success($deployment);
    } catch (Throwable $e) {
        $stream->append("\n\033[31m✖ {$e->getMessage()}\033[0m\n");
        $this->finish($deployment, 'failed', $e->getCode() ?: 1);
        $this->github->failure($deployment);
    } finally {
        $lock->release();
    }
}

private function runScript(Site $site, OutputStream $stream): ProcessResult
{
    $this->files->write($site->deployScriptPath(), $site->deploy_script, 0700);   // via beacon-fs

    // `bash -eo pipefail` → first failing line aborts; a pipeline failure is not
    // swallowed by the last command's status.
    // GNU timeout kills the whole process group; oomExpendable marks the build
    // as the OOM killer's first victim so mysqld is never chosen (audit §0.3).
    $result = $this->runner->asSite(
        argv: ['/usr/bin/timeout', '--foreground', '--kill-after=10s', self::SCRIPT_TIMEOUT.'s',
               '/bin/bash', '-eo', 'pipefail', $site->deployScriptPath()],
        cwd: $site->path,
        env: $this->deployEnvironment($site),
        timeout: self::SCRIPT_TIMEOUT + 30,
        stream: $stream,
        oomExpendable: true,
    );

    if ($result->failed()) {
        throw new DeploymentFailedException(
            "Deployment script exited with code {$result->exitCode()}.", $result->exitCode() ?: 1);
    }

    return $result;
}

/** @return array<string,string> — injected into every deploy script (spec §2.5) */
private function deployEnvironment(Site $site): array
{
    $node = $site->node_version
        ? "/usr/local/node/v{$site->node_version}/bin"
        : '/usr/local/node/default/bin';

    return array_filter([
        'BEACON_SITE'     => $site->name,
        'BEACON_SITE_DIR' => $site->path,
        'BEACON_BRANCH'   => (string) $site->repository_branch,
        'BEACON_PHP'      => $site->php_version ? "/usr/bin/php{$site->php_version}" : null,
        'BEACON_COMPOSER' => '/usr/local/bin/composer',
        'BEACON_NODE'     => "{$node}/node",
        'BEACON_NPM'      => "{$node}/npm",
        'BEACON_NPX'      => "{$node}/npx",
        'BEACON_BUN'      => '/usr/local/bun/default/bin/bun',
        'BEACON_PM'       => $site->package_manager === 'bun'
            ? '/usr/local/bun/default/bin/bun' : "{$node}/npm",
        'BEACON_PORT'     => $site->proxy_port ? (string) $site->proxy_port : null,

        // Cap V8's heap at ~65% of physical RAM. This is what actually prevents
        // the OOM kill — swap only softens the landing (audit §0.3).
        'NODE_OPTIONS'    => '--max-old-space-size='.MemoryBudget::nodeHeapMb(),

        'PATH' => "{$node}:/usr/local/bun/default/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin",
        'HOME' => '/home/beacon', 'USER' => 'beacon',
        'CI' => 'true', 'NODE_ENV' => 'production',
        'COMPOSER_HOME' => '/home/beacon/.composer',
    ]);
}
```

**Default deploy scripts** (`DeployScriptFactory`), seeded per type and fully editable:

```bash
# Laravel
cd $BEACON_SITE_DIR
$BEACON_COMPOSER install --no-interaction --prefer-dist --optimize-autoloader --no-dev
[ -f package.json ] && { $BEACON_NPM ci || $BEACON_NPM install; $BEACON_NPM run build; }
$BEACON_PHP artisan migrate --force
$BEACON_PHP artisan storage:link || true
$BEACON_PHP artisan optimize
$BEACON_PHP artisan queue:restart
```

```bash
# Next.js / Nuxt / Static — identical shape, differing only in build output
cd $BEACON_SITE_DIR
$BEACON_PM install --frozen-lockfile || $BEACON_PM install
$BEACON_PM run build
```

### 4.6 Live output: the `OutputStream` contract (Reverb-ready)

```php
interface OutputStream {
    public function append(string $chunk): void;
    public function close(): void;
}
```

- **`FileOutputStream`** — appends to `/var/log/beacon/{deployments,commands}/<uuid>.log`, written by the panel itself. Crash-safe, survives page reload.
- **`LogTail::read($path, int $offset)`** → `['offset' => int, 'chunk' => string, 'eof' => bool]`.
- **Polling** `GET /sites/{site}/deployments/{deployment}/log?offset=N` → `{ offset, chunk, status, duration_ms }`. React polls at 1 s while `status ∈ {queued, running}`.
- **Reverb later**: a `BroadcastingOutputStream` decorator also fires `DeploymentOutputReceived`; the polling endpoint stays as the backfill path. **No UI change** — the terminal reconciles by byte offset.

### 4.7 Web Console execution flow

Per spec §7: from the site root, as `beacon`, hard 120 s cap.

```php
// App\Jobs\RunSiteCommand — queued, so a 2-minute command never occupies an FPM worker
$result = $this->runner->asSite(
    argv: ['/usr/bin/timeout', '--foreground', '--kill-after=5s', '120s',
           '/bin/bash', '-lc', $this->command->command],
    cwd: $site->path,                      // /home/beacon/example.com
    env: $this->deployEnvironment($site),
    timeout: 130,                          // Symfony backstop behind GNU timeout
    stream: $stream,
);

$this->command->update([
    'status' => match (true) {
        $result->exitCode() === 124 => 'timed_out',   // GNU timeout's deadline code
        $result->successful()       => 'success',
        default                     => 'failed',
    },
    'exit_code' => $result->exitCode(),
]);
```

Exit code `124` is how the UI distinguishes ⏱️ **Timed Out** from ❌ **Failed**.

### 4.8 `ServerMetricsService` — no shelling out

The spec suggests `top`/`free`/`df`. Parsing those is fragile across locales and slow (`top -bn1` sleeps). Reading `/proc` is exact, locale-proof and ~100× cheaper:

| Metric | Source |
|---|---|
| CPU % | two reads of `/proc/stat` 200 ms apart → `1 − Δidle/Δtotal` |
| RAM | `/proc/meminfo` → `MemTotal − MemAvailable` (`free` alone over-reports cache) |
| Swap | `/proc/meminfo` `SwapTotal`/`SwapFree` |
| Disk | `disk_free_space('/')` / `disk_total_space('/')` — pure PHP |
| Uptime | `/proc/uptime` |
| Load | `sys_getloadavg()` |
| Service state | `systemctl show -p ActiveState,SubState,MainPID --value <unit>` — **no sudo** |

Cached 2 s for the dashboard poll; `PollServerMetrics` writes a row every minute for sparklines. The panel's own pool must **not** set `open_basedir` or `disk_free_space` fails — enforced by `HealthCheckService`.

### 4.9 GitHub: App-level webhooks + polling fallback (audit §0.4)

```php
class WebhookReachability
{
    /**
     * A GitHub App has ONE webhook, configured at App level — not per repo.
     * Rev 1 wrongly created per-repo hooks. Moving the panel to a domain later
     * therefore means PATCHing the App's hook config, not touching any repo.
     */
    public function refresh(GithubInstallation $installation): void
    {
        $url = route('webhooks.github');                       // absolute, from APP_URL

        if ($installation->webhook_url !== $url) {
            $this->client->patchAppHookConfig($installation, ['url' => $url]);  // JWT-authed
            $installation->update(['webhook_url' => $url]);
        }

        // Read GitHub's OWN record of delivery outcomes — never assume success
        $deliveries = $this->client->listAppHookDeliveries($installation);
        $latest     = $deliveries[0] ?? null;

        $installation->update([
            'webhook_reachable'    => $latest !== null && $latest['status_code'] < 400,
            'last_delivery_at'     => $latest['delivered_at'] ?? null,
            'last_delivery_status' => $latest['status_code'] ?? null,
        ]);
    }

    /** Public HTTPS on a resolvable name — GitHub will not trust a self-signed :8443 cert. */
    public function canReceiveWebhooks(Server $server): bool
    {
        return filled($server->panel_domain)
            && $server->panel_url_public
            && ! filter_var($server->panel_domain, FILTER_VALIDATE_IP);
    }
}
```

**UI behaviour — the feature is never silently broken and never removed:**

| Panel state | Auto-Deploy control |
|---|---|
| Public domain + valid LE cert | **Push webhooks.** Deliveries panel shows real status codes + Redeliver |
| IP / self-signed / behind NAT | **Poll mode**, selected automatically. Inline note: *"Auto-deploy is running in polling mode (checks every minute). Attach a panel domain for instant push deploys →"* |
| Webhook configured but last delivery ≥ 400 | Amber banner with the actual status code, Redeliver button, and a one-click **Switch to polling** |

```php
// App\Jobs\PollRepositoryHeads — every minute, only for sites with deploy_trigger = 'poll'
$sha = $this->git->remoteHead($site);          // git ls-remote <repo> refs/heads/<branch>

if ($sha !== null && $sha !== $site->last_polled_sha) {
    $site->update(['last_polled_sha' => $sha, 'last_polled_at' => now()]);

    if ($site->auto_deploy && $site->last_polled_sha !== null) {   // skip the first observation
        DeploymentService::queue($site, trigger: 'poll', sha: $sha);
    }
}
```

This also gives GitLab, Bitbucket and self-hosted Git full auto-deploy with **zero inbound ingress** — a capability Rev 1 did not have. `insecure_ssl` is never enabled on the App.

Other GitHub pieces: `GitHubAppClient` (RS256 JWT → `POST /app/installations/{id}/access_tokens`, cached 50 min), `GitHubManifestFlow` (self-POSTing form to `https://github.com/settings/apps/new?state=…`, then `POST /app-manifests/{code}/conversions` — one click, no manual credential entry), `DeploymentStatusReporter` (Deployments + Commit Statuses ⏳/✅/❌ deep-linking back to Beacon's log page).

`POST /webhooks/github` is stateless and session-free, guarded by `VerifyGitHubSignature` (`hash_equals('sha256='.hash_hmac('sha256', $raw, $secret), $header)`), filters by `repository.full_name`, records a `webhook_deliveries` row, and returns `202` in milliseconds.

### 4.10 `MySqlService` — least-privilege admin (audit §0.5)

```sql
-- install.sh, run once as root over the unix socket.
-- Deliberately NOT `GRANT ALL ON *.*`: that carries FILE, PROCESS, RELOAD,
-- SHUTDOWN, SUPER and CREATE TABLESPACE, none of which Beacon needs.
CREATE USER 'beacon_admin'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY '<generated-32-byte>';

-- Static privileges. GRANT OPTION is mandatory: MySQL only lets you grant
-- privileges you hold, and beacon_admin must pass these on to site DB users.
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, CREATE, DROP, INDEX, ALTER, REFERENCES,
      CREATE TEMPORARY TABLES, LOCK TABLES, EXECUTE, CREATE VIEW, SHOW VIEW,
      CREATE ROUTINE, ALTER ROUTINE, EVENT, TRIGGER, SHOW DATABASES
  ON *.* TO 'beacon_admin'@'localhost' WITH GRANT OPTION;

-- CREATE USER also covers DROP USER, RENAME USER, ALTER USER and REVOKE ALL.
-- BACKUP_ADMIN is REQUIRED: since 8.0.21, `mysqldump --single-transaction`
-- issues LOCK INSTANCE FOR BACKUP. Without it every backup fails.
GRANT CREATE USER, BACKUP_ADMIN ON *.* TO 'beacon_admin'@'localhost';

-- NOT granted: FILE, PROCESS, RELOAD, SHUTDOWN, SUPER, CREATE TABLESPACE,
-- REPLICATION SLAVE/CLIENT, and every *_ADMIN dynamic privilege.
-- No FLUSH PRIVILEGES needed — MySQL 8 applies GRANT/REVOKE immediately.
```

```ini
# /etc/mysql/mysql.conf.d/99-beacon.cnf
bind-address     = 127.0.0.1     # never on the network; UFW never opens 3306
secure_file_priv = NULL          # disables LOAD DATA INFILE / SELECT INTO OUTFILE outright
local_infile     = OFF           # blocks the malicious-server client-file-read attack
```

Connection and query rules:

- The panel connects **over the unix socket** (`/var/run/mysqld/mysqld.sock`) on a second Laravel connection (`mysql_admin`). The credential is unusable over TCP.
- Site DB users are created as `'user'@'localhost'`, never `'%'`.
- Site grants use `ON \`db\`.*` — `ALL` scoped to one database **cannot** include `FILE` (global-only) or `GRANT OPTION`, so it is safe by construction.
- **Identifiers cannot be bound.** `SqlIdentifier::quote()` enforces `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,64}$` and wraps in backticks with internal backticks doubled. Passwords in `CREATE USER … IDENTIFIED BY` are **string literals**, which `PDO::quote()` escapes correctly against the connection charset.
- Backups: `mysqldump --single-transaction --quick --no-tablespaces --routines --triggers` — `--no-tablespaces` is what keeps `PROCESS` off the required list.

### 4.11 Swap & memory provisioning (audit §0.3)

```bash
# install.sh — idempotent, filesystem-aware
ram_mb=$(awk '/MemTotal/{print int($2/1024)}' /proc/meminfo)

if [[ -z "$(swapon --show --noheadings)" && "$ram_mb" -lt 4096 ]]; then
    swap_mb=$(( ram_mb * 2 )); (( swap_mb < 2048 )) && swap_mb=2048
    (( swap_mb > 4096 )) && swap_mb=4096

    avail_mb=$(df --output=avail -m / | tail -1)
    if (( avail_mb > swap_mb + 5120 )); then          # keep 5 GB headroom
        fstype=$(findmnt -no FSTYPE /)
        if [[ "$fstype" == "btrfs" ]]; then
            truncate -s 0 /swapfile && chattr +C /swapfile   # btrfs swap requires nodatacow
        fi
        fallocate -l "${swap_mb}M" /swapfile 2>/dev/null \
            || dd if=/dev/zero of=/swapfile bs=1M count="$swap_mb" status=none
        chmod 600 /swapfile && mkswap /swapfile >/dev/null && swapon /swapfile
        grep -q '^/swapfile' /etc/fstab || echo '/swapfile none swap sw,nofail 0 0' >> /etc/fstab
        printf 'vm.swappiness=10\nvm.vfs_cache_pressure=50\n' > /etc/sysctl.d/99-beacon.conf
        sysctl -q --system
    else
        echo "WARN: not enough free disk for a ${swap_mb}MB swapfile — skipping" >&2
    fi
fi

# Critical services become the LAST OOM victims (builds become the first, §1.9)
for unit in mysql redis-server nginx php8.3-fpm; do
    install -d "/etc/systemd/system/${unit}.service.d"
    printf '[Service]\nOOMScoreAdjust=-500\n' > "/etc/systemd/system/${unit}.service.d/99-beacon-oom.conf"
done
systemctl daemon-reload
```

`MemoryBudget::nodeHeapMb()` returns `max(512, floor(MemTotalMb × 0.65))`, feeding `NODE_OPTIONS`. The site create/deploy UI warns when a Next.js/Nuxt build is attempted with less than 2 GB of RAM + swap combined.

### 4.12 Other services in brief

- **`CertbotService`** — `certonly --webroot -w /var/www/beacon-acme --agree-tos -n -m <email> --cert-name <primary> -d …`; parses `certbot certificates`; installs `/etc/letsencrypt/renewal-hooks/deploy/beacon.sh` → `systemctl reload nginx`. A daily job re-syncs `expires_at` and warns under 14 days.
- **`SupervisorService`** — render → `beacon-supervisor write` (stdin, content-validated) → `reread-update` → `start`. `status()` parses `supervisorctl status`.
- **`CronService::sync()`** — regenerates the managed block from `cron_jobs`, writes via `beacon-cron write`, preserving lines outside the markers.
- **`HealthCheckService`** — asserts wrapper ownership/mode, sudoers presence, **that `beacon` has no sudoers entry**, that `/opt/beacon/panel/current` is root-owned, Redis reachability, swap presence on small hosts, and disk headroom. Any failure raises a red banner.

